\frac{4}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{3}((\\frac{\\pi}{4})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "584e96b6-767c-5e14-899f-41a99d429ed3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677094} {:answer/id #uuid "78ee06fb-d3bd-5699-be5d-99abba240a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677108} {:answer/id #uuid "b534102c-0a28-5ffc-8498-8c551bd0cc23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677141} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8e45df-9845-509b-a95f-6c7724735b22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677158} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0beb08-add5-50bf-82af-696f8e97dadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\pi}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b534102c-0a28-5ffc-8498-8c551bd0cc23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677141} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f94dbd-24b0-502c-8bef-8dd471a94ea1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677153}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a4a4dc8e-8a02-5ef0-a5ce-5526bba8d539" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{36 - 6 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{36 - 6 x^{2}}=\\sqrt{36(1-(\\frac{1}{6})x^{2})}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{6} x}{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\sqrt{6})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6})(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2})=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x=\\sqrt{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6})(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth transformed endpoints lie strictly between $-1$ and $1$, so the integrand is continuous throughout the interval.\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{36 - 6 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{5}{6}\\int_{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{\\sqrt{6} x}{6})^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{5}{6}(\\sqrt{6})\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{5 \\sqrt{6}}{6}\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{5 \\sqrt{6}}{6}[\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\\\  &= \\frac{5 \\sqrt{6}}{6}(\\operatorname{arcsin}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  &= \\frac{5 \\sqrt{6}}{6}((\\frac{\\pi}{4})-(\\frac{\\pi}{6})) \\\\  &= \\frac{5 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{72}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677131 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a0125b7-63f0-5ffe-9867-939dcd35b2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a0125b7-63f0-5ffe-9867-939dcd35b2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677070} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3ea9054-3361-5bd8-b506-dcb0dcac388a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677185}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7b41060-9701-5ac8-9406-41c43c4a9895" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{9}} \\frac{9}{81 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=9 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=9,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{9})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=(9)(0)=0 \\\\ x=\\frac{1}{9}&\\Longrightarrow u=(9)(\\frac{1}{9})=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{9}} \\frac{9}{81 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 9\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{9}} \\frac{1}{1+(9 x)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 9(\\frac{1}{9})\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 1\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 1[\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  &= 1(\\operatorname{arctan}(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}(0)) \\\\  &= 1((\\frac{\\pi}{4})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677142 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d602eba-c683-5422-ab3f-d225478a529e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d602eba-c683-5422-ab3f-d225478a529e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677098} :answer-field/id #uuid "56821200-ef2e-57da-b433-e28f4b7b7183" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677092}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b68941c7-a358-52a8-9847-bc887dddfa00" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{7}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{2}} \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{49 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{49 - x^{2}}=\\sqrt{49(1-(\\frac{1}{49})x^{2})}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{x}{7}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{7},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(7)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{7}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{7})(- \\frac{7}{2})=- \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x=\\frac{7}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{7})(\\frac{7}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth transformed endpoints lie strictly between $-1$ and $1$, so the integrand is continuous throughout the interval.\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{- \\frac{7}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{2}} \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{49 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{6}{7}\\int_{- \\frac{7}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{7})^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{6}{7}(7)\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 6\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 6[\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  &= 6(\\operatorname{arcsin}(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}(- \\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  &= 6((\\frac{\\pi}{6})-(- \\frac{\\pi}{6})) \\\\  &= 2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193240cb-9bf1-5fc3-88c4-343eb2b3f61c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{256}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677056} {:answer/id #uuid "2303c723-3669-5376-b718-f0b6719d1697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{288}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677061} {:answer/id #uuid "3e412948-a45d-5098-9434-a82895c83f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{96}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677084} {:answer/id #uuid "b3fa66f7-e082-5e62-acfc-3e26bc6ee6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677139} {:answer/id #uuid "b40c90ad-24fd-5084-80a0-31c0f725200f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{2048}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e412948-a45d-5098-9434-a82895c83f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{96}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677084} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7792e2b-87fe-5b28-8d18-1c100112100d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677130}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b7e7efd8-4daf-5a99-9901-08530da7dbd2" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{8}{3}}^{\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{3}{3 x^{2} + 64}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n3 x^{2} + 64=64(1+(\\frac{3}{64})x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{8}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{8}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8})(\\frac{8}{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ x=\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8})(\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3})=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{\\frac{8}{3}}^{\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{3}{3 x^{2} + 64}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{64}\\int_{\\frac{8}{3}}^{\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{1+(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{8})^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{64}(\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3})\\int_{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{1} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\int_{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{1} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}[\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{1} \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}(\\operatorname{arctan}(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}((\\frac{\\pi}{4})-(\\frac{\\pi}{6})) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{96}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af8cc77-0bac-5940-b352-f949e5f99a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1af8cc77-0bac-5940-b352-f949e5f99a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677057} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee451c8-40b1-5552-b4a2-16770a8b9dcd" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677050}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8833921-cd55-5d33-86f3-5cb87a7b71f5" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{10}} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 - 25 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=5 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=(5)(0)=0 \\\\ x=\\frac{1}{10}&\\Longrightarrow u=(5)(\\frac{1}{10})=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth transformed endpoints lie strictly between $-1$ and $1$, so the integrand is continuous throughout the interval.\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{10}} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 - 25 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 2\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{10}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5 x)^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 2(\\frac{1}{5})\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2}{5}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2}{5}[\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  &= \\frac{2}{5}(\\operatorname{arcsin}(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{2}{5}((\\frac{\\pi}{6})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\pi}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de17d22-ce4a-560a-97da-52aa819f6d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1de17d22-ce4a-560a-97da-52aa819f6d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677058} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b06cdcb-17e2-5614-8223-3a8a95be3cd8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677113}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8ad7c5d-7e92-54a2-a9ba-2d3f25475100" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{6}{x^{2} + 64}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 64=64(1+(\\frac{1}{64})x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{x}{8}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(8)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{8})(0)=0 \\\\ x=\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{8})(\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{0}^{\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{6}{x^{2} + 64}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{32}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{1+(\\frac{x}{8})^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{32}(8)\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{4}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{arctan}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{4}((\\frac{\\pi}{6})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\pi}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2759c9ed-11ea-57ee-a0bd-9ad257122f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2759c9ed-11ea-57ee-a0bd-9ad257122f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677065} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fcc298a-078c-5c60-b6a2-c6d4172da034" :answer-field/key "coefficient" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677120} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccc64ea2-8f5a-54f2-9e68-90e50c57bc59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccc64ea2-8f5a-54f2-9e68-90e50c57bc59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677163} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5f1fd37-720c-5104-aaf1-071e70b68d8c" :answer-field/key "argument" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677188}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5ffb59e-2be0-5b32-8138-13035a607668" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2}{9}} \\frac{5}{81 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{coefficient}} $\\operatorname{arctan}($ {{argument}} $)$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=9 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=9,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{9})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=(9)(0)=0 \\\\ x=\\frac{2}{9}&\\Longrightarrow u=(9)(\\frac{2}{9})=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{0}^{\\frac{2}{9}} \\frac{5}{81 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 5\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2}{9}} \\frac{1}{1+(9 x)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 5(\\frac{1}{9})\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{5}{9}\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{5}{9}[\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  &= \\frac{5}{9}(\\operatorname{arctan}(2)-\\operatorname{arctan}(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{5}{9}((\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(2 \\right)})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{5 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(2 \\right)}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094fa516-728f-5be6-a4fe-f67ece9b8145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "094fa516-728f-5be6-a4fe-f67ece9b8145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677047} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee3d0bc0-f989-584a-ae0f-e17e36f20d73" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677190}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d97ef683-6715-5e81-a7d1-14b2ffc5e533" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}}^{\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{9 - 6 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - 6 x^{2}}=\\sqrt{9(1-(\\frac{2}{3})x^{2})}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{6} x}{3}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3})(- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4})=- \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3})(\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth transformed endpoints lie strictly between $-1$ and $1$, so the integrand is continuous throughout the interval.\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}}^{\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{9 - 6 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 3\\int_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}}^{\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{\\sqrt{6} x}{3})^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 3(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2})\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3 \\sqrt{6}}{2}\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3 \\sqrt{6}}{2}[\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\  &= \\frac{3 \\sqrt{6}}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}(- \\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  &= \\frac{3 \\sqrt{6}}{2}((\\frac{\\pi}{3})-(- \\frac{\\pi}{6})) \\\\  &= \\frac{3 \\sqrt{6} \\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3879e69e-611a-5e48-af0d-b81d5085eba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{288}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677081} {:answer/id #uuid "3c73aab7-f56a-5357-b2cd-6c75dfe0e5f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677083} {:answer/id #uuid "40638152-c07a-5845-b659-ed194dc93945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677086} {:answer/id #uuid "48f997ef-3952-5d82-987d-59ddad9a4ab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677088} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5a079d-39a5-5990-8353-75942f5fb50c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40638152-c07a-5845-b659-ed194dc93945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677086} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3205561-4844-5231-9a76-4b12f71b281e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677191}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e13e5fe8-8cb3-5e53-84d4-dc9d70dae4ca" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{6} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 36=36(1+(\\frac{1}{36})x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(6)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{6})(0)=0 \\\\ x=6&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{6})(6)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{0}^{6} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{12}\\int_{0}^{6} \\frac{1}{1+(\\frac{x}{6})^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{12}(6)\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{2}\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arctan}(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{2}((\\frac{\\pi}{4})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\pi}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "168d4392-e6c0-51c7-a965-acadc2514a1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677055} {:answer/id #uuid "5f917a32-7963-5d6f-afcc-c9a117beb131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677099} {:answer/id #uuid "8b30ca6b-ec84-5558-804b-cffd2d66e216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677114} {:answer/id #uuid "ced38559-d73a-5251-a64c-bdd66fd6d35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677166} {:answer/id #uuid "dbaa1cec-9fad-5c4c-9b41-008695f4e480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b30ca6b-ec84-5558-804b-cffd2d66e216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677114} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5c43e5-3673-5b00-8930-97762031a8dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1c5c6fb-e670-586e-8a39-d5d94b3f065f" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{16}} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1 - 64 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=8 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=8,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{8})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=(8)(0)=0 \\\\ x=\\frac{1}{16}&\\Longrightarrow u=(8)(\\frac{1}{16})=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth transformed endpoints lie strictly between $-1$ and $1$, so the integrand is continuous throughout the interval.\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{16}} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1 - 64 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 3\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{16}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(8 x)^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 3(\\frac{1}{8})\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{8}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{8}[\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{8}(\\operatorname{arcsin}(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{8}((\\frac{\\pi}{6})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\pi}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2afd7b19-eca2-5ee6-b883-ba3c32d3c286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677071} {:answer/id #uuid "33b3be47-676e-5ece-9ce1-37cd7674fbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{6} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677074} {:answer/id #uuid "3684568f-217d-59ef-b6af-389c35869a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6} \\pi}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677080} {:answer/id #uuid "759e5427-78c7-5cb9-aa97-0a52c8ecd3d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677105} {:answer/id #uuid "77ebe17d-2513-5cde-ae28-8040113f8496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77ebe17d-2513-5cde-ae28-8040113f8496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677107} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f025f07-d47b-5049-b3e3-da3e27c754f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e251937d-16b7-5326-a140-cdc3ea29c25f" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{3 \\sqrt{2}} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 6=6(1+(\\frac{1}{6})x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{6} x}{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\sqrt{6})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6})(0)=0 \\\\ x=3 \\sqrt{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6})(3 \\sqrt{2})=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{0}^{3 \\sqrt{2}} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{3}\\int_{0}^{3 \\sqrt{2}} \\frac{1}{1+(\\frac{\\sqrt{6} x}{6})^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{3}(\\sqrt{6})\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}[\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}((\\frac{\\pi}{3})-(0)) \\\\  &= \\frac{\\sqrt{6} \\pi}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "123e3224-f470-5a1e-9a86-1c2e4cc2a51e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677053} {:answer/id #uuid "2227dc7c-2cb7-5aee-aa2f-3b4d2b7a95d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677060} {:answer/id #uuid "8b7753d6-ba04-5328-ac31-33c61adfc066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677115} {:answer/id #uuid "8d780d79-735a-5941-8c9f-4801469c84c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677117} {:answer/id #uuid "ddae6bea-2729-582d-a153-7fc9cd6edc01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddae6bea-2729-582d-a153-7fc9cd6edc01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677176} :answer-field/id #uuid "90be1365-ed16-5813-b9ee-ed8cc6b8c2ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677122}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e4cdc649-5543-52c4-9e7e-a603083141ff" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{36 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{36 - x^{2}}=\\sqrt{36(1-(\\frac{1}{36})x^{2})}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(6)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds using the same substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-3&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{6})(-3)=- \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x=3&\\Longrightarrow u=(\\frac{1}{6})(3)=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth transformed endpoints lie strictly between $-1$ and $1$, so the integrand is continuous throughout the interval.\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{36 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{3}\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{6})^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{3}(6)\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 2\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 2[\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  &= 2(\\operatorname{arcsin}(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}(- \\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  &= 2((\\frac{\\pi}{6})-(- \\frac{\\pi}{6})) \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "974f4491-1b3e-5162-8762-b997c2ce7d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974f4491-1b3e-5162-8762-b997c2ce7d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679152} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b20481d-efa0-5d19-bace-b463c668fb4a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679143}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2276b7cb-4dac-5fe2-bb8d-8f1bf4683a99" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 2=\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-2&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec72688-32e4-5656-8061-411a0927fe7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679137} {:answer/id #uuid "727b8260-3d14-5059-9672-3775c19345fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679138} {:answer/id #uuid "821019bb-4994-56a5-8447-9fcd89362852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679146} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6b489b-2030-5270-bbbd-cd07e0af5b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679160} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa3533c-cdd8-5b93-8b50-a2595b657296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ec72688-32e4-5656-8061-411a0927fe7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679137} :answer-field/id #uuid "455b54ae-fb4e-51b4-9b57-73bd4b9e1f9d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679121}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31e905b6-c251-53f6-8de0-854ce3af6324" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{8}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{1}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{8}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19912f7a-c635-5395-99a4-013d98b0d958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19912f7a-c635-5395-99a4-013d98b0d958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679111} :answer-field/id #uuid "be16bb1a-f6f4-5233-8a1c-d8524f048c88" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679171}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3de4a265-dec4-55ca-a9f1-ffb48c66ba45" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4=2$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-2&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47cd604e-5003-5beb-a4a5-d9d85cb9390f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47cd604e-5003-5beb-a4a5-d9d85cb9390f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679123} :answer-field/id #uuid "e94e8786-71eb-5b21-8a20-50168f744c66" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679194}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "45114a62-33d3-51ec-a7c8-28ce8b3500fa" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 9=9\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-3&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=3&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21197bf9-2b81-5ac7-8c46-599b9dd9fed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21197bf9-2b81-5ac7-8c46-599b9dd9fed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679112} :answer-field/id #uuid "c55102e2-8ac3-5c1e-9026-690c0be8c3ee" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679179}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b0acf8e-9b1e-5ef1-915d-3d20f3467d5a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 4=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b59afd9-f2c2-5e5e-9970-6f992e37ea86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679133} {:answer/id #uuid "9ead6177-d303-5cab-b8ea-a5219cccb094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679158} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ec166a-a9bc-539d-9701-76c30fbff55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\