e :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{1}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{4}} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 - 4 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd50c84e-e76e-5b86-9c45-33afb043d39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd50c84e-e76e-5b86-9c45-33afb043d39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679182} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7e8cf9-9c61-5b9f-a08a-ea419798d119" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679124}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6dc4c518-ea77-5d68-9ae9-a019b2654d65" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "655b0f49-fcfd-5ba2-beeb-83411fb11bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "655b0f49-fcfd-5ba2-beeb-83411fb11bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679131} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a3de38-19e2-573b-8df5-7b7b7688a564" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679176}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c04b91e-e6f9-52ef-8ef4-38b49a786e88" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bdd67e1-4beb-54d3-b9e9-eeb6ff9c2b12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679156} {:answer/id #uuid "d67390ab-7f56-5eab-9802-08b91490b693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679186} {:answer/id #uuid "dff3c3ba-174c-59a9-a7d6-ee62a42838cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679192} {:answer/id #uuid "feb487a8-0c5d-5079-a216-cdadbac5ce2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679208} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc45760-e969-5f79-a809-324f6b4539a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffc45760-e969-5f79-a809-324f6b4539a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679209} :answer-field/id #uuid "dda9ad6d-761a-5204-abdd-09a476b38691" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679190}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8165fa70-1166-5f10-bb32-499a1e0700ee" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{4}} \\frac{2}{16 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{1}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{4}} \\frac{2}{16 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4442b25-4856-563c-a354-75d5a7986c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4442b25-4856-563c-a354-75d5a7986c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679165} :answer-field/id #uuid "7417936b-d70e-5012-b79b-d3dccd8da46b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679139}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8acbeaf6-4a49-5cff-9bbf-1d990a1f3203" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2=3$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=3\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "752d5c38-aae6-5338-ab74-b34f77ca7581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "752d5c38-aae6-5338-ab74-b34f77ca7581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679141} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e7ca9e-841b-531b-a4f0-3cbddc3883f2" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679197}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d454498-8e2d-5fa9-93ca-5a57d26ac575" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{4} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 16=16\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{4})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=4&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{4} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{8}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbc4eb12-c082-533c-91e3-42088827c6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbc4eb12-c082-533c-91e3-42088827c6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679167} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ba04b5-b93a-5fbf-9837-f370a0a1420d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679201}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98784736-c266-5208-a6fc-c447c86d139a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 2=2$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-1&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0fc0013-4555-5cdc-9e01-c62bff3e2ff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0fc0013-4555-5cdc-9e01-c62bff3e2ff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679159} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdbaa2de-b165-5834-a0ac-d39437261aa1" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679170}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aca9c0da-bf9d-5af9-86af-aa07acdced2e" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{3} \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 9=9\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot 3=\\frac{4}{3}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=3&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{3} \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d5b975-d657-53f4-8d36-078f875960bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679108} {:answer/id #uuid "4f1fbc1f-a7b4-5aa0-aab7-92081dbdffa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #e