al is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12033083-b770-5f99-9be0-0a3495fb33a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679110} {:answer/id #uuid "524bda8a-9e74-5c2b-8175-d014bc04c2f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679126} {:answer/id #uuid "5d231189-769b-5732-ace7-6461f3b15312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679129} {:answer/id #uuid "8bbc0e95-7b5c-52aa-905d-f8b75261fa33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679148} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4fd602-fb90-5466-9105-9362a34b9033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d231189-769b-5732-ace7-6461f3b15312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679129} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd745591-a33f-5a52-85b2-efc8a2030b08" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679206}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1eadd6c-be48-5b89-8213-8431b738e7d5" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=2 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{3}{4 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{1}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{3}{4 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4ce1593-21be-58fe-8716-c7cdedf915f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ce1593-21be-58fe-8716-c7cdedf915f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679199} :answer-field/id #uuid "3787a9f0-915a-565d-803f-d861322f1a32" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbf8ae14-6723-512f-93e9-c8784d3ce601" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{6}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c91e4652-47f8-5671-81db-f5c918eefb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c91e4652-47f8-5671-81db-f5c918eefb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679181} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7619d5-798e-51ec-a379-94d0401eb97d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bc78c8a6-488e-51bf-ac0e-c24a6281e74a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-4}^{4} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 16=16\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{4})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{16}\\cdot 4=\\frac{3}{4}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-4&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=4&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-4}^{4} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e842c11-c7f3-564f-a933-92803d029ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679118} {:answer/id #uuid "47a44f18-f0ce-55ca-b079-1064dd752f1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679122} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8d094b-7bda-5af9-9605-694b68421bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679150} {:answer/id #uuid "dafbb5d3-917d-5770-b4cd-9a5425b2287f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679188} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ca9f8b-2271-5493-9c33-abecf2b359aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id 