tion.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c4726a49-36ea-5eb2-a7dd-f6af9ac558b8" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2=3$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-1&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=3\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\pi.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d97abc82-4a04-5bc5-ad2b-ec73cfff0c85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97abc82-4a04-5bc5-ad2b-ec73cfff0c85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679187} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c988bbf-80f6-580d-b23c-9d777dfb2dbc" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id