ight)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683038 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "266c1cae-3692-5924-96cb-117702847d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "266c1cae-3692-5924-96cb-117702847d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683017} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f7df34-3e6d-5955-94fe-963eee69c65a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683032}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3d5756b-44e6-5fa5-a82f-9cefb144862a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 2=2$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-1&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "240331fe-77e6-5e07-bbd7-7c3036a7406d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "240331fe-77e6-5e07-bbd7-7c3036a7406d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683016} :answer-field/id #uuid "0564ed71-add6-5e7d-9cef-0e7fccbf5758" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683009}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0a31a52-2d0e-58b1-8e5c-8873975ed4b7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{6}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683043 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb93ae60-1314-5c1b-8b18-5be2bf67f2c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb93ae60-1314-5c1b-8b18-5be2bf67f2c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683052} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e7c9b3d-a38a-5b2d-8d31-027e6df341be" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683018}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3a16373-f0d4-5113-bf47-986eb7d7132a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2=3$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathr