hrm{d}x=2 \\sqrt{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 2 \\sqrt{2}=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{8 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7644753-abd6-5ed7-a994-0f807b480077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7644753-abd6-5ed7-a994-0f807b480077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693132} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3b1e437-277c-50aa-93b5-e24edf0fcc97" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693151}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a481085-117b-5999-ad76-8e19a57728c7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 12}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{6}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 12=12\\left(1+(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{6})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2 \\sqrt{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 2 \\sqrt{3}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-2&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 12}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd2d16ed-0a22-517d-aff0-2fc17e5cbd6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd2d16ed-0a22-517d-aff0-2fc17e5cbd6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693136} :answer-field/id #uuid "1749ef1b-b7dd-5332-b751-7e02c047f761" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693063}] :question/difficulty {:db/iden