$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{6}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "524fb952-2eab-5a48-87d8-266780ca5971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "524fb952-2eab-5a48-87d8-266780ca5971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693086} :answer-field/id #uuid "8872060e-15bf-590a-bf77-9b4df5106182" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fa48c8e-d2b6-5eba-8ad3-f816664db3eb" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{25 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - x^{2}}=5\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{5})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=5\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 5=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{25 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\