\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{1}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{4 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{8}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ede60e48-9cdd-536f-b441-48e9615792ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ede60e48-9cdd-536f-b441-48e9615792ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693148} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4e0a536-3443-5d5d-926c-ef349b9c9b62" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693145}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5286232-dcfd-5ef5-b3e2-5f7420d2ca2f" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-4}^{4} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 16=16\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{4})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-4&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=4&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-4}^{4} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a22543-28d5-5089-8691-a57799840d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57a22543-28d5-5089-8691-a57799840d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693088} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f2fd66c-c278-5547-a2e0-a6c78f6e834b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693067}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba24a3c5-0af8-5f12-bad0-104365814844" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize 