rked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2 - x^{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7abc9f-93c1-51ac-91c8-84d0387c912a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a7abc9f-93c1-51ac-91c8-84d0387c912a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693057} :answer-field/id #uuid "66395239-5556-58ae-96ea-5eb4b32ef4c7" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693096}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d5f42ff5-5444-50e8-91bf-056a3b48e465" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 3=3\\left(1+(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{18}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce6bc08f-8eed-50f7-8ce0-d6396cded99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce6bc08f-8eed-50f7-8ce0-d6396cded99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693137} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e4c11c1-503a-5f4e-9d8b-b90474f087ce" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693094}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e99bd3d1-b2c7-55da-9169-4f058c9afd0b" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{5} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 25=25\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{5})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=5\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{2}{25}\\cdot 5=\\frac{2}{5}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=5&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{5} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{2}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{2}{5}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{10}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b7e900f-58c5-54d9-b4dd-e9243a1038d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b7e900f-58c5-54d9-b4dd-e9243a1038d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693066} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2b6a189-cc62-5331-bc4a-c392adb11139" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f52e547a-67c6-54a7-8d53-a6934739d311" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{3} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 3=3\\left(1+(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\\\x=3&\\Longrightarrow u=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(\\sqrt{3} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e701470-541f-54c9-848a-ee3d9b95cc24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693074} {:answer/id #uuid "5e28e1d9-264a-54ea-853a-9204d1d56ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693093} {:answer/id #uuid "67743a5e-33fa-5aa0-