t(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{0}\\right)=\\frac{2}{5}\\left(\\left(0\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{10}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c05537-9374-58af-a715-f7a705fc094b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693268} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3a44cd-1747-52b8-a876-8ab8bc0ed490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693272} {:answer/id #uuid "b7feefbe-f2c8-5d86-bf8a-13e789771c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693289} {:answer/id #uuid "e95de0fd-da01-5165-9a66-2a661872263d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693295} {:answer/id #uuid "fde4d329-11e7-5509-bf35-3fb7fd46d6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12c05537-9374-58af-a715-f7a705fc094b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693268} :answer-field/id #uuid "c42f8ad8-4651-5513-9fbd-2913f823f2d0" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7267bef-6d93-518d-a40c-208d304f6659" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{1}{5}}^{0} \\frac{3}{25 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the exact value." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=5 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(5)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $3\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{3}{5}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{1}{5}&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{1}{5}}^{0} \\frac{3}{25 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\int_{-1}^{0} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{0}\\right)=\\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\left(0\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 \\pi}{20}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57774871-e260-5b20-86fa-bd7cb372a1e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693277} {:answer/id #uuid "6238d0b8-0cf6-5bc6-a0cc-de1db18b84bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693278} {:answer/id #uuid "87ef638d-a179-5b05-8715-a7e1291a2a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693280} {:answer/id #uuid "93c96896-41d8-541b-8c8d-073254646c67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693283} {:answer/id #uuid "d9aab288-d8e6-561b-8aea-db8ec6606ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93c96896-41d8-541b-8c8d-073254646c67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693283} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0393e59-d30d-54b5-8d80-335e9242475a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693294}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2526946-63b0-5d4c-935e-2bd3ace075e1" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\frac{3}{9 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the exact value." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{1}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\frac{3}{9 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Definite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Trigonometric Functions"}]}
